# systemd-homed allocates our uid out of the 60001..60513 range and keeps
# no /etc/passwd row for it, so getpwuid(60006) resolves only through
# nss-systemd. A nixpkgs-glibc binary can't dlopen the host's
# libnss_systemd.so.2, so ssh from git's own closure dies at startup with
# "No user exists for uid 60006" -- every ssh remote, not just this forge.
# git execs the openssh baked into its closure rather than PATH's, so
# putting the host ssh first in PATH does nothing; core.sshCommand is the
# only lever. The host binary links the host glibc and resolves fine.
// lib.optionalAttrs (!isDarwin) {
  sshCommand = "/usr/bin/ssh";
};

